---
# Generated from the page list rather than by jekyll-sitemap: that plugin
# builds its URL set before polyglot localises anything, so it emitted the
# 148 default-language URLs and none of the English ones.
#
# sitemap: false keeps this file out of its own output. The URL is also in
# _config.yml's exclude_from_localization so there is no stray /en/sitemap.xml
# claiming to be a second sitemap.
permalink: /sitemap.xml
sitemap: false
---
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9">
{%- assign default_lang = site.default_lang | default: 'en' -%}
{%- comment -%}
  Redirect stubs are skipped on purpose. jekyll-redirect-from marks them
  `sitemap: false` too, but they are where most of the duplicates in the
  Search Console report come from, so filtering on `redirect` as well keeps
  them out even if the flag is ever dropped. 88 of them ship.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- for p in site.pages -%}
{%- if p.url == '/sitemap.xml' or p.redirect or p.sitemap == false -%}
{%- continue -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- comment -%}
  site.pages is not only HTML: Sass emits /assets/css/style.css as a page
  and so does the /redirects.json lookup table. Directory URLs (the root, or
  any index) and .html documents are the only things worth listing.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign p_last_char = p.url | slice: -1, 1 -%}
{%- unless p_last_char == '/' or p.url contains '.html' -%}
{%- continue -%}
{%- endunless -%}
{%- include sitemap-entry.html url=p.url -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- for d in site.documents -%}
{%- if d.sitemap == false -%}
{%- continue -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- include sitemap-entry.html url=d.url -%}
{%- endfor -%}
</urlset>
